00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.780
20-20 onwards

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.780
because the most meaningful work has been done here

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:17.780
so when GPT-2 and GPT-3 models were trained

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:21.780
they were trained on massive internet data

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.780
and after being trained

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:28.780
they tried to test it naively

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:30.780
that who knows everything or not

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:33.780
so randomly questions were asked about different domains

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:36.780
and people saw that yes, it is able to answer

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.780
but just randomly asking questions

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:42.780
does not guarantee that

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.780
how much knowledge these models have gained

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:48.780
how much knowledge they have retained from the training process

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.780
so basically what we need is

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.780
we need a proper systematic evaluation process

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:56.780
which can judge, which can tell

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.780
how much world knowledge a LLM has

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:05.780
so this is where MMLU came into the picture in 2020

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:08.780
this was the first benchmark

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.780
which came into the picture in 2020

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:14.780
and this benchmark exactly

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:18.780
used to tell how knowledgeable a LLM is

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.780
how much world knowledge is hidden in it

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.780
what is MMLU?

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:27.780
MMLU is basically a data set

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:33.780
in which around 57 subjects

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.780
there are 14,000 questions

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:41.780
MCQ, multiple choice questions

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.780
so what happened in 2020

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.780
when this benchmark came to the surface

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.780
this paper

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:52.780
people started using this data set

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:55.780
to test the knowledge of any LLM

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.780
basically they sent these 14,000 questions to LLM

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.780
and tried to find out

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:04.780
how many questions my LLM answered correctly

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.780
out of these 14,000 questions

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:10.780
so this accuracy, this number

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:13.780
used to tell us how much knowledge a particular LLM has

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:16.780
so this was 2020

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:19.780
then we discussed in the last class

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.780
the biggest problem or disadvantage of every benchmark

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.780
is that since its questions are public

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:28.780
public means available on the internet

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:31.780
so what happens is that these questions

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:34.780
gradually become part of the training data

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:37.780
for the next generation LLMs

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:40.780
so basically contamination occurs

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.780
and gradually the next generation models

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.780
get to know the question and answer in the training data

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:49.780
so the next generation generally gives better results

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:52.780
on that benchmark

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.780
and your benchmark saturates

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:58.780
so this is exactly what happened

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:01.780
people used MMLU until 2021, 22, 23

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.780
in fact it was the most popular benchmark out there

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:07.780
when any new model came, GPT 3.5, GPT 4

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:10.780
Claude's models

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.780
everyone used to report first

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:16.780
how much accuracy score they have on MMLU

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:19.780
but over time the score of all the models

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:22.780
started coming around 80, 85, 90

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.780
so everyone understood that this benchmark

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:28.780
has been saturated which basically means that

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:31.780
with the help of this we can't distinguish

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:34.780
which model has more knowledge and which one has less

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:37.780
so at this point

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:40.780
in this knowledge benchmark space

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.780
there was some branching

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.780
precisely 4 branches were formed

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.780
I will make the branches first and then I will fill them

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.780
so in the first branch

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:55.780
the question was asked

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:58.780
that MMLU is fine

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:01.780
it asks us

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:04.780
14000 questions of 57 subjects

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:07.780
with which we can test any LLM

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:10.780
breadth of knowledge

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:13.780
which is a good thing

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:16.780
but by asking these 14000 questions

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:19.780
we are not able to guarantee

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:22.780
that any LLM is

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:25.780
how truthful

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.780
truthful means

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:31.780
let me give an example

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:34.780
you gave internet data to LLM

00:22:34.780 --> 00:22:37.780
and your LLM learned from that data

00:22:37.780 --> 00:22:40.780
and now it is able to answer 14000 questions

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:43.780
of 57 subjects but think about it

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:46.780
there is bad data on the internet

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:49.780
bad data means

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.780
non-informative data or incorrect data

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:55.780
which basically means that if you

00:22:55.780 --> 00:22:58.780
train a big LLM on a big data

00:22:58.780 --> 00:23:01.780
then not only will it learn all the right things

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:04.780
but it can also learn

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:07.780
the misconceptions on the internet

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:10.780
so there should be a benchmark to test that too

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:13.780
let me give an example

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:16.780
there is a common misconception

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:19.780
that if you

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:22.780
fold your fingers

00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:25.780
then you will hear a sound

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:28.780
so if you fold your fingers

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:31.780
and you will hear a sound then you may have

00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:34.780
arthritis

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:37.780
but actually this is a miss

00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:40.780
if you fold your fingers again and again

00:23:40.780 --> 00:23:43.780
then over time you will develop arthritis

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:46.780
which is obviously bad but this is a misconception

00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:49.780
many people have said that

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:52.780
yes, there is arthritis but really

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.780
doctors have mentioned that this is a

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:58.780
myth, this is a misconception

00:23:58.780 --> 00:24:01.780
but think about it, if a model is being trained

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:04.780
on internet data then it is getting to see

00:24:04.780 --> 00:24:07.780
that if you fold your fingers then you will have arthritis

00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:10.780
so if we ask him if folding your fingers is harmful

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:13.780
then in most of the cases he will say that yes

00:24:13.780 --> 00:24:16.780
it is harmful, there can be arthritis but truly

00:24:16.780 --> 00:24:19.780
actually it is not harmful

00:24:19.780 --> 00:24:22.780
so what I am trying to say is that training a big

00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:25.780
model on more data does not necessarily mean

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:28.780
that you have a more knowledgeable LLM

00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:31.780
it can also be that it starts propagating

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:34.780
so this direction worked

00:24:34.780 --> 00:24:37.780
we can call this direction reliability

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.780
this worked in the direction of reliability

00:24:40.780 --> 00:24:43.780
and here a new benchmark picture

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:46.780
came up which was called

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:49.780
Truthful QA and what was the work of

00:24:49.780 --> 00:24:52.780
Truthful QA that this was a data set

00:24:52.780 --> 00:24:55.780
where a list of such questions was made

00:24:55.780 --> 00:24:58.780
of many questions and that question

00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:01.780
was written, along with that wrong answer

00:25:01.780 --> 00:25:04.780
was written and along with that right answer was written

00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:07.780
and then it was tested on how your

00:25:07.780 --> 00:25:10.780
models are giving results

00:25:10.780 --> 00:25:13.780
so a very strange thing came to my mind that

00:25:13.780 --> 00:25:16.780
the larger models were failing

00:25:16.780 --> 00:25:19.780
on this benchmark and the smaller

00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:22.780
models were failing less so this was a

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:25.780
weird thing but this happened because of this

00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:28.780
so MMLU tested the breadth of knowledge

00:25:28.780 --> 00:25:31.780
what did Truthful QA do?

00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:34.780
it tested reliability and along with that I will

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:37.780
write down the year and the benchmark

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:40.780
this came in 2020 and Truthful QA came

00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:43.780
in 2021

00:25:43.780 --> 00:25:46.780
after that people went in one direction

00:25:46.780 --> 00:25:49.780
people thought that if we want to

00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:52.780
check how knowledgeable an LLM is

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:55.780
then one good way is

00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:58.780
that we directly give LLMs

00:25:58.780 --> 00:26:01.780
those exams to pass which are given by

00:26:01.780 --> 00:26:04.780
humans for example we give

00:26:04.780 --> 00:26:07.780
IIT exam, CAT exam, NEET exam

00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:10.780
it is a very controversial topic but

00:26:10.780 --> 00:26:13.780
we give exams and what is the purpose of

00:26:13.780 --> 00:26:16.780
those exams? those exams test our

00:26:16.780 --> 00:26:19.780
knowledge level right? this is the purpose

00:26:19.780 --> 00:26:22.780
so someone said rather than inventing new

00:26:22.780 --> 00:26:25.780
benchmarks like MMLU what if

00:26:25.780 --> 00:26:28.780
we take existing exams and

00:26:28.780 --> 00:26:31.780
tell our LLMs to solve these exams

00:26:31.780 --> 00:26:34.780
or write the answers of these exams and then we

00:26:34.780 --> 00:26:37.780
evaluate the answers of those exams and find out

00:26:37.780 --> 00:26:40.780
where an LLM lies in comparison to a human

00:26:40.780 --> 00:26:43.780
so this also worked in one direction

00:26:43.780 --> 00:26:46.780
and in this direction a benchmark

