along with this five more example questions

00:47:14.780 --> 00:47:17.780
will be sent and your model

00:47:17.780 --> 00:47:20.780
will tell you the correct answer A, B, C, D

00:47:20.780 --> 00:47:23.780
and then you have to flip it over

00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:26.780
and measure the accuracy score

00:47:26.780 --> 00:47:29.780
there are 14000 questions, how many out of them

00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:32.780
the model has answered correctly, that is the accuracy score

00:47:32.780 --> 00:47:35.780
its simple, very straight forward

00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:38.780
now here one thing is different that there are two ways of scoring

00:47:38.780 --> 00:47:41.780
one is that your model will look at the question

00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:44.780
and will print a character

00:47:44.780 --> 00:47:47.780
A, B, C, D

00:47:47.780 --> 00:47:50.780
obviously, second option is that

00:47:50.780 --> 00:47:53.780
you don't generate anything from the model

00:47:53.780 --> 00:47:56.780
instead you get its log probabilities

00:47:56.780 --> 00:47:59.780
that how much probability it is assigning to A

00:47:59.780 --> 00:48:02.780
how much probability it is assigning to B

00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:05.780
how much probability it is assigning to C

00:48:05.780 --> 00:48:08.780
and how much probability it is assigning to D

00:48:08.780 --> 00:48:11.780
and the one whose probability is assigning the most, we will consider that as the answer

00:48:11.780 --> 00:48:14.780
you might be knowing if you have studied transformer architecture

00:48:14.780 --> 00:48:17.780
that whenever you have to predict a token

00:48:17.780 --> 00:48:20.780
you assign a probability against every token

00:48:20.780 --> 00:48:23.780
in your entire search space

00:48:23.780 --> 00:48:26.780
we get the log of that probability

00:48:26.780 --> 00:48:29.780
and we find out who is being told the answer

00:48:29.780 --> 00:48:32.780
so these two things are done, either you generate the answer directly

00:48:32.780 --> 00:48:35.780
or you find out its log likelihood

00:48:35.780 --> 00:48:38.780
that who is being considered most probable in A, B, C, D

00:48:38.780 --> 00:48:41.780
and these two methods are used

00:48:41.780 --> 00:48:44.780
in MMLU and generally

00:48:44.780 --> 00:48:47.780
the same answer is not given from both of them

00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:50.780
there is a difference of 1 to 3 points

